PATH RECONCILIATION (only deviation from the literal prompt path)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated output path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Maps/**` does NOT exist in this repo
and is NOT a project.yml source group. The iOS/macOS app targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-
primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no
`TeslaSync/Features`. The repo's real, compiled canonical feature home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/
<Domain>/**`, where all 71 sibling P7 pages ship (Admin, Analytics, Battery, Charging, Driving, …) and
which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Maps`. Strings
ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is
the same reconciliation the sibling AuditLog / DiskForecast / SchemaDrift logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is `/navigation`, which resolves to the maps domain. The existing
`AppRoute.maps` case (pathSegment `maps`, Vehicle group, icon `mappin.and.ellipse`) is the host;
`AppRouteParser` already aliases `/location` → `.maps` and now also `/navigation` → `.maps`, and
`NavigationRouteRegistration` registers `NavigationRoutePage` on `.maps`, chained into `\.routeHosts`
in TeslaSyncApp.swift. The page is reachable via the Vehicle-group sidebar entry and any `/navigation`
or `/location` deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

